The flag is **`-s`** (long form **`--slurp`**).

From `jq --help`:

```
-s, --slurp               read all inputs into an array and use it as
                          the single input value;
```

Example:

```bash
$ echo '{"a":1} {"a":2}' | jq -s .
[
  {
    "a": 1
  },
  {
    "a": 2
  }
]
```

Without `-s`, jq would apply the filter to each input value separately; with `-s`, all inputs are collected into a single array first.
